%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ef4a382a350f98438c21cfd3c789fdf, type: 3}
  m_Name: AtariDirection
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lessonTitle: Atari Direction
  lessonId: ataridirection
  slides:
  - slideName: Slide 1
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: When you put an opponent's stone or group of stones in Atari, they
      will most likely try to save it.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 2
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In some situations, however, the direction of where you put your opponent's
      stones in Atari to will actually determine whether they live or get captured.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 3
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Here, for example, black has two spots to choose from in order to put
      the highlighted white stone in Atari.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 4
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: If black goes at 1, white would try to escape by going at 2. Notice
      how white can now very easily connect with its other stones.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 5
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: However, if black goes at 2, white would try to escape by going at
      1, but is immediately greeted by more black stones.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 6
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In the end, it is impossible for white to escape and is captured by
      black when it goes at the highlighted location.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 7
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Put the singular white stone in Atari towards the best direction.
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: b9d07a9783814ed42accda9b1bcea41f, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 8
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Put the appropriate group of white stones in Atari towards the best
      direction.
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: bcffdee7a5e2afa4fbbba85d7948e2c2, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 9
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Put the appropriate group of white stones in Atari towards the best
      direction.
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 4fd5e3129af77b84eb5144f2b2b4a123, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 10
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Remember how there are no liberties at the edges of the board? You
      can use that to your advantage as well when putting your opponent in Atari.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 11
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: 'Take a look at the highlighted white stones. There are two directions
      black can put then in Atari towards: up towards more white stones ot right
      towards the edge.'
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 12
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: If black goes at 1, white escapes by going at 2. It even puts one of
      black's stones in Atari in this case. Ouch!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 13
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: However, if black goes at 2, white would try to escape by going at
      1, but immediately bumps into the edge, losing a liberty.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 2
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 14
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: In the end again, it is impossible for white to escape and is captured
      by black when it goes at the highlighted location.
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 0}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 15
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Put the appropriate group of white stones in Atari towards the best
      direction.
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 60540c1c1fe441243ae73f3b885e99bf, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 16
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Put the appropriate group of white stones in Atari towards the best
      direction.
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 58ad236ae9ec5454785ad7d3405bce63, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 17
    slideType: 1
    bodyText: Put the appropriate group of white stones in Atari towards the best
      direction. Look out, white may try to escape!
    boardSource: 0
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 3e839d17d7fdd5a458c1284235d564a3, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 9
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
  - slideName: Slide 18
    slideType: 0
    bodyText: Great job this lesson. Now you know how to use Atari with strategy.
      See you in the next ones where we will learn about techniques of capture!
    boardSource: 1
    boardJsonFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 3e839d17d7fdd5a458c1284235d564a3, type: 3}
    inlineBoardSize: 7
    inlineCurrentPlayer: 1
    inlineBoardFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationTypeFlat: 
    inlineAnnotationNumberFlat: 
    correctYesAnswer: 1
    correctNumberAnswer: 0
